    "summary": "IBAN format errors in payment data cause refund transaction failures, prompting customers to inquire about refund status. [E-02] Payment-db records show five recent refund failures with status FAILED_IBAN_FORMAT (E-02), while ticket-db shows a median response time of 2 hours, well within the 24‑hour SLA (E-01). The release introduces mandatory IBAN format validation at the point of payment data entry (or as a pre‑refund step) for the refund payments data asset (DA‑PAY). The release is approved because it directly removes the root cause, satisfies the success criterion of zero IBAN‑format failures per week, and no blocking issues were identified. The total volume of refund attempts is unknown, so the failure rate cannot yet be calculated (U‑UNKNOWN‑01), and other possible data quality issues contributing to refund failures have not been examined (U‑UNKNOWN‑02).",
